Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.790 align:start position:0%
 
sometimes even the most talented horror  actors choose to hang up their hats and  leave the industry eventually  no matter how much they loved making  their movies working in hollywood for  any period of time can be enough to burn  anybody out john franklin rose to  prominence in the horror world when he  starred as  isaac the creepy young cult preacher in  1984's children of the corn  he went on to land a small role in  1988's child's play and  later played cousin it in the adams  family and adam's family values  he could have easily continued acting  but the unexpected loss of two loved  ones caused him to question whether or  not he  really wanted to keep working in showbiz  and after the events of september 11th  2001 he realized that he needed to take  his life in a new direction  so he looked in the mirror and asked  himself what his legacy was  i've entertained you know millions of  years but is that  all that i want written on my tombstone  or my obituary  franklin decided that he needed to take  a break and shortly after this  realization he responded to an  ad for a teaching job he spent over a  decade in the classroom which allowed  him to combine his various passions by  teaching english  and screenwriting among other subjects  today franklin is slowly returning to  acting by taking on parts as he sees fit  though he isn't pursuing those roles  full time  farouza bach gave an eerily convincing  performance as the powerful and  vengeful young witch nancy in 1996's the  craft  as she starred alongside fellow witches  nev campbell robin tunney and rachel  true  the movie is beloved as a cult favorite  and it seemed like bulk could have had a  bright future in horror films but she  never quite fulfilled that promise  looking back she says she simply wasn't  interested in chasing fame  in 2013 she told dread central i never  just want to work for the sake of  working  there has to be something there for me  so that i can grow from the experience  i've never just taken a job because i  wanted the check i struggled a lot with  being pushed too hard in my 20s with  people telling me that i had to keep  taking more and more movies because  that's really only when i'd be relevant  like one of my favorite movies ever is  the craft but i'm sure you get that all  the time  of course but i know we're far removed  from that with no desire to be the  flavor of the moment  bach has instead focused on finding  roles that she can truly feel passionate  about  adrian king is best known for playing  alice hardy in the original friday the  13th  but off screen she had a horrifying  experience that pushed her out of the  public eye for years  she had no idea that shortly after  rising to fame she would be forced to  deal with a real situation that was far  scarier than anything in her movie  career for a year and a half she was  followed by a stalker who pursued her  for a bizarre reason  as he claimed that king reminded him of  someone who had wronged him in the past  unfortunately the authorities initially  dismissed king's claims  she stated that the police even  attempted to place the blame on her for  acting in such a scary movie  king later met with the makers of friday  the 13th part 2 and arranged for her  character to be killed off  as she told uproxx in 2015 i couldn't  handle doing another film and dealing  with what no one else seemed to want to  deal with  it was worse because we didn't know who  the stalker was and it was drawn out and  this person was so brilliant  it really kind of spun me into a very  weird place  king eventually pivoted to voice over  work so that she could keep acting  without appearing on screen  she now primarily works as a winemaker  and artist  michael myers the infamous masked  murderer of the halloween franchise  is one of the most famous villains in  horror movie history  he was played by nick castle in the 1978  original  although you probably wouldn't recognize  him behind the mask you also won't  notice him credited as an actor in many  other movies although he did return for  the 2018 reboot  and he signed on for its sequels while  he walked into a fantastic opportunity  when he was offered the role of michael  myers he never  intended to become an actor in fact he  always dreamed of writing and directing  his own films  so how did castle end up with this  iconic role despite his lack of interest  in acting  as it turns out he and halloween  director john carpenter were close  friends in film school  and after carpenter achieved some early  success he knew that he could help give  castle a career boost so the two of them  teamed up for halloween and castle got  to learn the ropes from a pro  s castle later told dread central the  reason i was doing it was just to hang  out on the set to learn how to become a  director  so it was a great experience for me and  you never know how things are going to  turn out  linda blair was a relative unknown with  little experience under her belt when  she landed the iconic role of regan  mcneil in 1973's the exorcist  her performance as a disturbed child  possessed by a demon is enough to make  anyone's skin crawl thanks to  unforgettable moments that involved head  spinning and split pea soup  blair appeared poised to use that  experience as a stepping stone to a long  and vibrant career but these days she  has a new set of priorities as she  dedicates most of her time to animal  rights activism  she became a vegetarian in 1988 and in  2001 she adopted  a fully vegan diet she's rescued many  stray dogs and she says that she feels a  kinship with these misunderstood animals  because of the way the media portrayed  her after the exorcist came out  in 2013 she told the sydney morning  herald  i realize these dogs are being portrayed  the same as i was  as a monster there was prejudice  misunderstanding and it was  being lied about so i became quite a  forceful speaker on their behalf  blair laments the fact that most  journalists only want to talk to her  about the exorcist rather than her  animal welfare work  as she put it i'm sad but i'm not mad at  them  that movie changed your life completely  but it gave you a megaphone  you didn't realize that for a while but  it gave you a megaphone  to to get your point across when he was  just eight years old david dorfman  starred as aiden in 2002's the ring  he captivated audiences with his  portrayal of a young boy with psychic  abilities whose family is tormented by a  ghostly entity  bent on revenge for the suffering she  endured in her life he also made an  appearance in the 2003 reboot of the  texas chainsaw massacre  while he certainly had the potential to  be a successful adult actor he hasn't  appeared in a film since 2010  ultimately he decided to take a  different path in life fortunately for  his sake it turns out that dorfman's  talents extend beyond acting  a brilliant student he was admitted to  harvard law school at an age when most  people were just starting their  bachelor's degrees  he managed to graduate at the top of his  class when he was only 21 and then  started building his legal career  in 2017 he told refinery29  i've been working as an attorney at  capitol hill in dc and then at one of  the top firms in hong kong i was really  fortunate to be at the justice  department in washington too  honestly i just feel so lucky to have  such interesting experiences  from hollywood to harvard i'm just  really incredibly grateful  for all these great opportunities you  might know devay chase from your  nightmares  she probably popped up there a few times  after she played the vengeful ghost  samara in the ring  the creepy image of a young girl with  black hair hanging in front of her face  could easily  haunt anyone for days not to mention she  made an entire generation dread picking  up the phone whenever it rings  chase didn't land too many other parts  following the ring but she definitely  stayed busy  she voiced lilo in the disney movie lilo  and stitch as well as the tv show based  on it and she also had a recurring part  on the hbo series big love  but recent legal troubles have left her  with an empty acting schedule for the  past few years  in november 2017 she was arrested when  she was caught driving a stolen car  then in 2018 she was arrested again this  time for possession of illegal drugs  whether or not chase chooses to return  to acting we hope she'll be able to get  back on her feet again and stay out of  trouble  if you're a horror hound you surely  remember heather langenkamp as nancy  thompson in the classic 1984 slasher  flick a nightmare on elm street  she started multiple films in the  durable franchise and she's always  spoken highly of the experience  to this day she insists she has no idea  why she was chosen for the role but she  still  feels honored and blessed that she had  the opportunity that was  nancy wes it's not me yeah but it was  you that gave nancy her strength  in 2018 langenkamp lost her teenage son  to brain cancer which prompted her to  take a step back from acting  in 2019 she told pop horror that's why i  haven't really been doing very much for  the last year  because i have been just recovering from  seven years of just real  real horror now that i've kind of moved  beyond that stage of my life i just  really appreciate  being alive and appreciating every gift  that i've been given  langenkamp still loves acting but these  days she's more interested in working on  short films  instead of features she also runs a  makeup effects company with her husband  in 1999's the blair witch project  heather donahue played a film student  who was downright obsessed with  capturing footage of the mysterious  title character  and who refused to turn off the camera  no matter what danger she encountered  the actress never expected that this  little low-budget found footage flick  would make the impact that it has  although the blair witch project drew in  large audiences and caused quite a stir  with its incredibly effective marketing  campaign  donahue's performance wasn't positively  received by everyone  in fact she even won a worst actress  award from the razzies  donahue has said that once the hubbub  over the blair witch project died down  she had a quote  firm lack of interest in appearing in  anything else despite  all the criticism she faced she didn't  give up on acting right away but she  eventually took her career in a  completely different direction when she  decided to begin growing medical  marijuana  she even wrote a memoir called grow girl  about her experiences with the drug  it became really obvious to me why we  have this  long intricate and sometimes dangerous  relationship with this plant  it's hard to believe that danny lloyd  had never acted before he played danny  torrence in 1980s the shining  his performance was so convincing that  it's easy to believe that he actually  had psychic powers  you may have wondered why he didn't go  on to appear in other films after  starring in such an iconic movie  despite his abundant talent he struggled  to land similar opportunities  he continued going on auditions but  aside from securing a role in a  made-for-tv movie about the watergate  scandal  he wasn't offered any parts that he was  interested in although he enjoyed acting  he eventually realized it was time to  leave the industry behind  in 2017 he told the guardian i'm quite  happy with how things went  really i feel like i pretty much hit the  lottery with the shining  i don't regret trying acting when i  decided to stop i don't regret that  either  lloyd grew up to work as a teacher one  who wisely tried to keep his previous  acting experience a secret from his  students to avoid classroom disruptions  however he did get back in front of the  camera one more time to make a cameo in  dr sleep  the 2019 sequel to the shining  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper 